    "note": "Transcribed by hand from the table of section 56 of the Wines of Marked Quality Regulation, as consolidated to 13 October 2026 (last amended 14 July 2025 by B.C. Reg. 118/2025): its 22 geographical indications, each name as column 1 writes it and its item number, and \"a subdivision of\" the indication column 1 names (the Okanagan Valley's thirteen, the Cowichan Valley of Vancouver Island). Every other indication lies in British Columbia, whose indication is the whole province. The areas are drawn on maps the table cites, not read here. Text reproduced under the King's Printer Licence of British Columbia; only its facts are taken. Points are OpenStreetMap's, approximately: the place of the name, or the town or lake a subdivision is named after (Summerland, Kelowna, Naramata, Skaha Lake; Shuswap Lake for the Shuswap, OpenStreetMap's place of that name being in the Kootenays), or else the indication it lies in."
